---
description: American English for user-facing copy. Legal pages stay as written.
alwaysApply: true
---

Plot's primary market is the United States. Write user-facing copy in American English (color, favorite, theater, organize, program, -ize verbs). That includes app and web UI, the marketing site, social posts, What's On, card text, alt text, and email.

Marketing content is for a US reader: US release dates, US streaming services, US references, and US date order (June 19, Friday, June 19). Do not localize marketing for Australia or the UK.

Legal pages stay as they are. Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, Community Standards, and other legal pages keep their current wording, including British spelling where they already use it.

Do not add new `regionalWords()` call sites or new entries in `packages/core/spelling.js`. Existing call sites stay until a ticket asks to sweep them. A new string is American spelling, written out.
